==Old Norse==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|non|hifinn}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|12th century Icelandic}} {{IPA|lang=non|/ˈhiminː/}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|non|gem-pro|*himinaz||cloud cover, sky}}. Cognate with {{etyl|ang|-}} {{m|ang|heofon}}, {{etyl|osx|-}} {{m|osx|hevan}}, {{etyl|got|-}} {{m|got|𐌷𐌹𐌼𐌹𐌽𐍃}}. Ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|non}} {{m|ine-pro|*ḱemen-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*ḱemer-||stone, cloud, sky}}.

===Noun===
{{non-noun|m|himins|himnar}}

# the [[heavens]], [[sky]]
#* ''Jóns saga'' 33, in '''1858''', [[w:Jón_Sigurðsson|J. Sigurðsson]], [[w:Guðbrandur_Vigfússon|G. Vigfússon]], ''Biskupa sögur'', Volume I. Copenhagen, page [http://books.google.com/books?id=py4PAAAAIAAJ&pg=PA245 245]:
#*: {{...}} var svá skirt veðr ok hreint, at hvergi sá ský á '''himni''' {{...}}
#*: {{...}} ''the weather was so clear and bright that there were no clouds in the '''sky''''' {{...}}
# {{context|Christianity, especially in the plural|lang=non}} the [[heaven]], [[paradise]]
#* ''Þorláks saga'' 6, in '''1858''', [[w:Jón_Sigurðsson|J. Sigurðsson]], [[w:Guðbrandur_Vigfússon|G. Vigfússon]], ''Biskupa sögur'', Volume I. Copenhagen, page [http://books.google.com/books?id=py4PAAAAIAAJ&pg=PA95 95]:
#*: {{...}} dýrki þér föður yðarn, þann er á '''himnum''' er.
#*: {{...}} ''worshipped thy Father, who is in '''heaven'''.''

